From c33d4ae4c0c7a841b107ec99efc26b55757a13ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: kwshm, host access to the pages of shmem files

Lets the JavaScript host read and write the pages of a guest shmem file
(a memfd or a file in /dev/shm) in place: the kernel runs in the direct
map, so those pages already lie in memory the host sees, and the driver
only tells it which pages a file occupies and holds them while the host
may look. The guest side stays standard.

An export is a file, or a page-aligned range of one, with an id. Its
folios are pinned with memfd_pin_folios() (FOLL_PIN with long-term
semantics, as udmabuf does), which also allocates holes, so every page
the host sees is the file's. A pinned folio cannot be migrated
(compaction's refcount freeze fails) and is not freed while pinned, even
after a truncation removes it from the file: the host may see stale
pages but never freed or reused ones. A check compares the file's size
and the held folios' mapping and index; a refresh pins the file's
current pages, announces them and only then unpins the old ones.

Exports come from the host by name (open or create a regular shmem file
in /dev/shm, refresh, check, close: requests queued by the host, raised
with WASM_IRQ_SHM (7), handled by a work item in the init mount
namespace) or from the guest by fd (ioctl KWSHM_IOC_EXPORT on
/dev/kwshm, include/uapi/linux/kwshm.h; the export dies with
KWSHM_IOC_RELEASE or with the file that made it).

Five imports, none of which suspends: wasm_driver_shm_init(req_size)
(< 0: no device; then nothing is registered or allocated),
wasm_driver_shm_request(buf, max), wasm_driver_shm_attach(id, flags,
gen, size, pages, npages) (the page list, copied during the call),
wasm_driver_shm_detach(id) and wasm_driver_shm_reply(tag, result).
